speechtext:
B.	That one day allotted according to Standing Order 62 for the period ending June 30, 1983 shall be allotted to consideration of the said motion, provided that the motion shall be that described in section A of this Order;
C.	That at the conclusion of the sitting on the day that the said motion is called for consideration pursuant to this Order the motion shall be deemed to have been referred to the Standing Committee on Justice and Legal Affairs;
D.	That the Committee shall report thereon no later than June 7, 1983;
E.	That the said report shall be disposed of in not more than one sitting day, no later than June 30, 1983;
F.	Provided that all motions made in consequence of this Order including those in consequence of any Committee report pursuant to this Order shall be proposed only by a Minister of the Crown.
That is the motion which I wished to put on the record.
